msgid "``hexagon_loadlinux_<suffix>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/cdsp.rst:40
msgid ""
"Boots a guest operating system written for the Hexagon VM interface. Despite "
"the name, it is not specific to Linux. H2 starts the guest from an image "
"that QEMU has placed at the ``-kernel`` address in the table above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/cdsp.rst:57
msgid "``hexagon_booter_<suffix>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/cdsp.rst:46
msgid ""
"Runs H2 user programs.  The booter creates a VM, loads a program that it "
"reads from the host through semihosting, and waits for the program to exit::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/cdsp.rst:50
msgid ""
"qemu-system-hexagon -M qcs6490-cdsp -serial stdio -display none \\\n"
"    -bios hexagon_booter_qcs6490_cdsp \\\n"
"    -semihosting-config enable=on,target=native,arg=booter,arg=prog.elf"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/cdsp.rst:54
msgid ""
"Programs are loaded at ``0xa2000000`` by default; the booter's ``--"
"guest_base`` option changes this (``arg=--help`` lists its options)."
msgstr ""

